WEBVTT

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:21.450
<b>Muhyo & Roji's
Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.530
Strange... Something's wrong.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.130
It's past 2:00, but it's not coming out.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.930
Relax, Shiratori Aya-san.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.520
Hey, you're safe with us here.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.420
B-But usually...

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.020
It's okay.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.140
That piano...

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.900
What happened to it?

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.940
It's covered in spirit traces.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.250
Spirit traces?!

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.700
<b>Article 3 
Talent</b>

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.300
Spirit traces?

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:29.400
I can't see anything, though...

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.820
Spirit traces are traces left behind 
when a spirit touches something.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.220
<b>Spirit Traces</b>

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.220
This piano...

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.530
is a really famous piano that was 
used by well-known composers.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:43.260
That's why my dad bought it for me.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:49.550
My parents are rarely home 
since they're always so busy,

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.400
so they thought I must be lonely...

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.820
I see...

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.400
That's why your parents still 
aren't home at this hour.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.190
In other words, you mean that 
piano is your babysitter?

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.910
Yes, for three years.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.040
And over those three years,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.420
you became so skilled that 
you were labeled a prodigy.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.540
<b>Shiratori Aya Wins Piano Competition</b>

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.420
<b>A world-class performance 
brimming with talent</b>

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.290
A prodigy? I'm not...

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.470
So you won the world selection competition,

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.300
<b>Piano concert by girl prodigy 
with once-in-a-lifetime talent</b>

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.300
<b>Girl Prodigy</b>

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:19.110
and that night...

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.220
At exactly 2:00 in the morning,

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:54.150
a black shadow was sitting at
 the piano in the hall downstairs...

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.840
I just had to do something.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.840
<b>Don't hesitate to come to us!</b>

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.840
So I called you.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.070
I haven't done anything wrong,

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.440
so why is this happening?

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.350
You're asking why?

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:16.520
Do you have any idea what 
people think of you?

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.530
You should know

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.030
that countless people look
 upon you with envy.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.780
Wealth...

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.790
Looks...

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.430
Talent and fame...

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:37.040
Who wouldn't envy you, 
when you have all that?

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.170
Th-That's...

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.300
But what does that have 
to do with the spirit?

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.020
Everything.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:48.050
Aya-san, you can't see it,

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:52.870
but the air is full of spirit energy 
emitted by living humans.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.810
Their joy, their hatred, their sadness...

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.860
Intense emotions create spirit energy,

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.120
but hatred in particular 
generates it in massive amounts.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.020
It's very rare,

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.400
Hatred

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:09.280
Vengeful Spirit

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:08.120
but a mass of it can aggregate 
to form a vengeful spirit

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.280
and attack people.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.650
Then I'm...

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.290
the target of a vengeful spirit?

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.090
Relax.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.570
It's a vengeful spirit, but it's born of 
the spirit energy of common folk.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:27.090
Dregs are still dregs, no matter 
how much of it there is.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:32.850
No matter how jealous they are or how 
hard they try, people with no talent

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:37.730
can never match up to a prodigy, 
and we're gonna teach them that.

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:49.640
I hate talentless people.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.700
Especially...

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.450
ones in disguise!

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.910
What's with this stupid 
flower print, anyway?!

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.770
What's your problem? It's perfect!

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:00.340
My super papier mâché technique at work.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.240
Hmph. This is stupid.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.720
Aw, come on! There's no way 
the spirit will notice us in these!

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.720
<i>Now that I think about it...</i>

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:14.220
<i>I really don't know anything about Muhyo.</i>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:21.230
<b>Magical Law</b>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:21.230
<b>Muhyo Toru Special</b>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:21.230
<b>The Youngest Executor Ever!</b>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:21.230
<b>Young Talent
 Appears!</b>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:21.230
<b>A Shock Wave Rattles the 
World of Magical Law!!</b>

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.890
<i>He's the youngest executor ever,</i>

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.520
<i>a young talent in the 
world of magical law...</i>

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.680
<i>That's about it.</i>

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.730
<b>Talent</b>

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.730
<i>Talent...</i>

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.750
<i>Why does it mean that much to him?</i>

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.240
What's the hold-up, assistant?!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.610
Uh, right!

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.330
3 Days Later

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.990
5 Days Later

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:39.080
8 Days Later

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.340
Muhyo, come on!

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.630
10 Days Later

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.350
What time is it?

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.630
It's 3:00...

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:50.490
She said it came out at 2:00 
every day for ten days.

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:53.000
Maybe it noticed us?

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:54.060
It's odd.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:54.760
Huh?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.280
It's obvious from the spirit traces 
that a vengeful spirit has been here,

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:01.880
but its actions are too methodical 
for a vengeful spirit.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.730
Could a simple mass of spirit 
energy consciously do that?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.150
There's no reason for it to 
show up at exactly 2 AM.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:13.160
It should just attack Aya and be 
done with it, but it doesn't.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.600
I don't get it.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.260
He fell asleep!

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:19.160
All right, fine.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.770
I'll keep watch myself.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:31.500
Hey, wake up.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.080
Hey!

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:36.840
Wh-What is it?!

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:38.920
What's the meaning of this?

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:39.680
Huh?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.690
H-Hey, that spirit...

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:47.320
It's tiny?

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:50.730
Tiny? Don't be ridiculous.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.060
One wrong move...

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:55.320
and you're dead.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:02.330
According to Magical Law...

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.340
Article 142,

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:13.660
M-My head's going to burst!

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:14.570
for the crime of "Unsolicited 
Mass Emission...

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:18.680
of... Spirit... Energy..."

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:23.440
Damn that piano!

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.770
<i>Talent is fleeting, anyway!</i>

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.190
<i>Just because she's kinda cute...</i>

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.770
<i>Her parents, too!</i>

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.700
Not bad, for a bunch of ordinary people.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.370
Stop!

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:43.300
Aya-san!

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:47.250
I just... I just...

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:50.500
like the piano, that's all!

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.300
Aya-san...

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.890
The piano's reverberation is 
drowning out the spirit voices...

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.010
Well done, Aya.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.640
That's not something you can 
do just by liking the piano.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.520
That talent of yours

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.020
is proof that you've been chosen by Heaven.

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:10.520
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:13.530
Muhyo!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:17.450
I sentence you to "Beelzebub's 
Treasure Chest"!

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.450
<b>Sentence: Beelzebub's Treasure Chest</b>

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.040
A thing as ugly as you...

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:29.670
will look perfect in Hell's collection.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.890
Aya-san? Aya-san!

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.690
Looks like she fell asleep.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.920
Must be relieved to be rid 
of that vengeful spirit.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.170
Oh, yeah.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.220
The spirit traces are gone, too.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.820
She can play the piano 
without any worries now.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.250
Got Questions About Spirits? Ask Us!
We Offer Consultations for Those Troubled by Spirits
The Muhyo Bureau of Supernatural Investigation 
Advertisement by: Kusano Jiro 

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:10.250
Oh, that's our flyer. Aya-san had a copy.

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:11.720
Look closely.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:12.500
Huh?

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.250
That's...

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:17.740
The black and white of the 
Magical Law mark are inverted!

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:22.110
I didn't hand out any like 
that! Why is it here?

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:24.440
This explains everything.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.520
Huh?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.790
That vengeful spirit's target wasn't Aya.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.020
It was me.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.270
What?

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:35.600
It used a fake flyer to get her to call me,

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:39.460
and when I trusted Aya's word that it 
would appear at 2:00, it attacked me.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:42.450
The inverted mark is the sign of a traitor.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.830
Sheesh, could they have 
been any more blatant?

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:46.450
Got Questions About Spirits? Ask Us!
We Offer Consultations for Those Troubled by Spirits
The Muhyo Bureau of Supernatural Investigation 
Advertisement by: Kusano Jiro 

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.120
B-But who would do that?

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:51.210
When I was still in training...

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:55.000
There was a magic lawyer 
I was good friends with.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:11:02.920
Although he got jealous of my talent 
and ran off to the dark side.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.930
That's why I can't stand ordinary people.

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:12.980
<i>Muhyo...</i>

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:23.990
<b>Beelzebub's Treasure Chest</b>

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.990
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:30.000
<b>The Devil's Shadow</b>

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.000
<b>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau of 
Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.750
<b>Muhyo Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.160
Delivery for you.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.750
Coming!

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.490
Thank you!

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:41.460
From the Magical Law Association, for me?

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:48.470
This is...

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:50.480
a magic-sealing pen!

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:54.230
"Dear Kusano Jiro-dono,

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:59.980
This letter serves as a summons to undertake 
the Association's Promotion Exam.

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:03.260
If you choose to take the test, you must 
come to Association Headquarters

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.240
accompanied by your office's executor,

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:09.830
and you must bring the magic-sealing 
pen found in this package."

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.310
Yes! I did it, Muhyo!

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:17.770
Now I can become a first-class secretary

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:20.880
and be freed from the second-class odd 
jobs like compiling files and making tea!

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.890
I'll get to do actual magical law work!

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.640
Not for three more years!

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.320
Ow...

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:29.370
Right. Let's keep this pen, though.

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:30.780
It'll come in handy.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:34.490
You're nowhere near ready 
for a promotion yet, trash.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.280
Hey, you two!

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:41.150
Sorry to interrupt.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:42.840
Oh, Nana-chan.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:45.470
You know we're not supposed 
to meet with past clients.

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:47.800
Yeah, yeah. Too late now.

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.160
Look! The picture came out great!

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:53.320
Get out.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:54.890
I'm going to sleep.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.670
Ah, wait! Wait!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.330
Don't say that!

00:12:58.330 --> 00:12:59.170
Look at this!

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.550
Is that...

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.930
I took this picture of a 
mother and child recently.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:09.760
See that black shadow up 
on the pedestrian bridge?

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.890
What has me worried is...

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:20.010
I hope that spirit isn't connected 
to the mother and child.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:29.300
If you want us to do a job for 
you, make a formal request.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:32.310
Beat it. I don't care 
about this dumb picture.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:38.580
Well, I'm sorry it's just a dumb picture!

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.590
So long, hypocrite!

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:45.610
Hmph!

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:52.590
Oh, man... Muhyo, are you sure you 
want to leave that spirit to—

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:53.350
Hey!

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.100
He's asleep.

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:57.700
<i>Muhyo...</i>

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.300
Nana-chan!

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:08.990
Wait!

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:15.120
Huh? Take you to the pedestrian 
bridge in the picture?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.370
Yeah. I'm a little curious now, too.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.880
Are you sure you'll be okay, Roji-kun?

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.880
Wh-What?

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:32.660
That apron looks good on you.

00:14:33.110 --> 00:14:34.310
Th-This is...

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:41.310
Look, I know I suck at this stuff, 
but I'm studying, little by little.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:45.320
And I don't want to put any 
more responsibility on Muhyo.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:50.320
It seems like something's really 
troubling him right now.

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:57.200
Although he got jealous of my talent 
and ran off to the dark side.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.010
So even if I'm useless, I—

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:01.210
Uh...

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.710
Good one! That face was perfect!

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.190
I'll take you to the pedestrian 
bridge or anywhere you want!

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.880
Come on! It's a bit of a walk.

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:12.970
Wait, you're empty-handed?

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.300
Wanna buy purifying salt 
or something on the way?

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:16.140
I'm fine!

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:18.280
I've got what I need.

00:15:19.010 --> 00:15:20.640
<i>The magic-sealing pen...</i>

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:25.390
<i>and the talismans for avoiding ghost 
confrontations that I wrote with it.</i>

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:26.650
<i>I'll use these,</i>

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.880
<i>make Muhyo recognize my abilities...</i>

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:31.000
<i>and go get that promotion!</i>

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:40.570
This is it?

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:41.670
Yeah.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.400
There's no one around.

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:50.300
Yeah, urban development failed in this area,

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:53.190
so it's sort of a ghost town, I guess.

00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:57.060
Are you okay, Roji-kun?

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.310
I'm going. Wait here, Nana-chan.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:03.000
No! I'm going with you!

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:06.900
To be honest, that's reassuring.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:10.630
Right? But the truth is that 
I didn't want to be alo—

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:17.680
<i>Stay calm...</i>

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:20.180
<i>Muhyo... What would Muhyo do?</i>

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.780
<i>Muhyo would waste no time 
invoking magical law</i>

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:26.430
<i>with his Art of Exorcism talismans.</i>

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:27.770
You two...

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.680
can see me?

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:33.130
Upsy-daisy...

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:37.930
You see, I fell from this pedestrian bridge.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:40.410
The wind was about to blow my hat off,

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:41.930
so I tried to grab it...

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:43.890
You can talk?!

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.470
And I've been here all by myself ever since.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:52.400
Wait just a sec. I'll come over there.

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:55.770
Hey, doesn't this spirit seem harmless?

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.910
Like my dad.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:01.910
Well, it's true there are 
cases like that, but...

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:04.440
No, wait, Nana-chan.

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:07.200
<i>That's right... Muhyo said...</i>

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:09.420
<i>that friendly spirits are...</i>

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:13.610
Listen. A spirit that seems
 chatty and clever

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:16.480
is one that's already devoid of reason.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.180
Nana-chan!

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.100
Huh?

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:21.680
Get down!

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:25.810
What's this?

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.310
You figured out I was lying?

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:30.690
You damn bound spirit! Take this!

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.410
Art of Exorcism!

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:37.580
What was that? Fireworks?

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:39.700
No way...

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:47.210
My first prey in so long!

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:47.210
No!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:50.210
Isn't this place great?

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:54.870
I can kill all the people I want and 
say they just fell down from here!

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:05.100
<i>I'm powerless.</i>

00:18:06.420 --> 00:18:08.520
I'm sorry, Nana-chan!

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:12.900
Hey, idiot.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.280
Think of the manual.

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:18.670
What makes the magic-sealing pen work?

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.370
That's right! It has to be 
immediately after it's written,

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.290
or it won't work!

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:35.920
Nana-chan!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:37.000
Well done.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.090
Muhyo...

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.660
Are you satisfied now that 
you can use the talismans?

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:45.600
But in this case, by acting 
without authorization,

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.100
you almost let Nana die.

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:53.130
Magical law doesn't exist to kill people.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:54.840
It exists to save them.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:59.240
Make sure you remember that, Kusano Jiro.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:02.490
You want to continue working 
in magical law, don't you?

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:04.990
Yes,

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:07.370
Executor Muhyo.

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:18.440
According to Magical Law Article 1624,

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.130
<b>Crime: Attempted Murder</b>

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:20.950
for the crime of "Attempted Murder"...

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:25.390
I sentence you to "The Devil's Hammer"!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.300
<b>Sentence: The Devil's Hammer</b>

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:36.150
With the next blow, you'll 
become part of Hell's soil.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.070
No!

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:41.660
Stop!

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:56.040
<b>Muhyo Bureau of Supernatural Investigation</b>

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:56.040
Muhyo, here.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.050
Huh? What's this about?

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:03.820
You said I can't take the exam 
for another three years, right?

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:05.700
You were right.

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:08.210
I was rushing things.

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:10.820
You seemed to be having a hard time,

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.120
and I wanted to help you somehow...

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:16.810
So I wanted to have my abilities 
acknowledged sooner.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.900
I can't apologize enough to Nana-chan.

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:23.780
<i>Oh, boy. It really was bothering him.</i>

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:26.700
<i>I came to tell him not to worry about me,</i>

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.270
<i>but I can't go in there now...</i>

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:29.700
I'm awful, aren't I?

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:32.040
But...

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:37.210
But I want to get much better and 
save people with... magical law...

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:38.820
Huh?

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:41.350
Well said.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.220
Huh?!

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:51.980
I'll remember you said that.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:55.770
Is that... the entrance to 
the Magical Law Association?

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.060
Let's get going.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.320
I have some business there, too.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:02.320
You mean... Muhyo!

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:07.370
Embarrass me over there and 
I'll send you to Hell—

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.100
Muhyo!

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.450
Thank you, Muhyo!

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:12.330
Give it a rest!

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:13.900
Just get ready!

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:16.080
Aye-aye, sir!

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.840
What?!

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:00.440
Let's learn about magical law!

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:00.440
(with video)

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:00.440
<b>Kusano Jiro 
"Celebrate? It's our first guest!"</b>

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:00.440
Subscribe

00:23:01.160 --> 00:23:02.700
LawTube!

00:23:02.700 --> 00:23:03.960
Just had to say that.

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:06.730
Today I'm gonna teach 
you the onion's secret.

00:23:08.490 --> 00:23:21.210
<b>Jabin</b>

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:10.940
The bean sprout told me this.

00:23:10.940 --> 00:23:13.770
After he uses magical law to 
vanquish a vengeful spirit,

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:17.230
this onion sleeps for three days!

00:23:17.230 --> 00:23:18.840
Talk about lame!

00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:21.550
Huh? Kenji-kun, what are you doing?

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:23.170
Gah! Bean sprout!

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.120
You can't just come in here.

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:26.460
If Muhyo wakes up, there'll be—

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:27.630
Ow!

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:29.970
(with video)

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:29.970
<b>Kusano Jiro 
"Celebrate? It's our first guest!"</b>

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:29.970
Subscribe

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:29.970
Why me?!

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:34.160
Western film style?

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:35.010
Dutch style?

00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:36.760
Japanese style?

00:23:36.760 --> 00:23:38.270
A well?

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:42.850
What's the deal with this mixed-up town?!

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:46.640
Next time on <i>Muhyo & Roji's Bureau 
of Supernatural Investigation</i>,

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:47.860
Article 4:

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:48.940
"Omen."

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:54.950
<b>Article 4 
Omen</b>

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:52.100
Magical law will be enforced.
